ANSWER: {"completedSection": "In case of a chemical spill, immediately identify the scenario by assessing the type and quantity of the spilled substance. Notify the supervisor and emergency response team immediately. Ensure all personnel in the vicinity don appropriate Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) as per the facility's PPE policy. Evacuate non-essential personnel from the area. Follow the spill response procedure specific to the chemical involved, utilizing spill kits and neutralizing agents where applicable. After containment and cleanup, ensure proper disposal of waste in accordance with hazardous waste regulations. Document the incident, actions taken, and any injuries or property damage. Conduct a debriefing with all involved personnel.

Communication Plan: Establish a clear chain of communication. The supervisor should inform the facility manager and safety officer. Use the facility's emergency communication system to alert all staff.

Drill Requirements: Conduct quarterly emergency spill response drills to ensure all personnel are familiar with procedures. Review and update the spill response plan annually or after any incident.", "references": "ISO 14001:2015, ISO 45001:2018, OSHA Hazardous Waste Operations and Emergency Response Standard (HAZWOPER)", "clauseAlignment": "This procedure aligns with ISO 14001 clause 8.2 by establishing operational controls for managing environmental aspects and emergency situations, and with ISO 45001 clause 8.2 by implementing processes to eliminate hazards and reduce OH&S risks, including emergency preparedness and response."}
